Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-05-02
Subject: Route parser local-verbosity cleanup through a pointer carrier
License: expat

`compiler/parser.pas` passes `current_settings.pmessage` as a `var`
parameter to `FreeLocalVerbosity`.  `current_settings` is a packed record
because it is serialized into PPUs, so the translated C++ bootstrap cannot
bind a non-const reference directly to that field.

Keep the packed `tsettings` layout unchanged, but copy the pointer field to
a local variable, let `FreeLocalVerbosity` update that local, then store the
result back into `current_settings.pmessage`.

--- a/compiler/parser.pas
+++ b/compiler/parser.pas
@@ -288,6 +288,7 @@
       var
          olddata : polddata;
          hp,hp2 : tmodule;
+         localpmessage : pmessagestaterecord;
        begin
          { parsing a procedure or declaration should be finished }
          if assigned(current_procinfo) then
@@ -521,7 +522,12 @@
            dec(compile_level);
            set_current_module(olddata^.old_current_module);
 
-           FreeLocalVerbosity(current_settings.pmessage);
+           { current_settings is a packed record.  Route the var parameter
+             through a local so the translated bootstrap does not have to
+             bind a reference directly to the packed field. }
+           localpmessage:=current_settings.pmessage;
+           FreeLocalVerbosity(localpmessage);
+           current_settings.pmessage:=localpmessage;
 
            dispose(olddata);
          end;
